  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer **mountain** array `arr` of length `n` where the values increase to a **peak element** and then decrease.\n\nOutput the index of the peak element.\n\nThe task is to solve it in `O(log(n))` time complexity.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** arr = [0,1,0]\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** arr = [0,2,1,0]\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** arr = [0,10,5,2]\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `3 <= arr.length <= 105`\n* `0 <= arr[i] <= 106`\n* `arr` is **guaranteed** to be a mountain array.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
